# Full asap-otap image — the ASAP-patched OTAP-Rust (`df_engine`)
# distribution with the unified `asap_sketches` processor wired into
# its `linkme` plugin registry. Phase 5 step D output (per
# docs/design-asap-otap-rust-integration.md §11 row D).
#
# ## Build model: host-build, container-ship
#
# Mirrors `Dockerfile.asap-otel` and the operator workflow Phase 4
# step D ships for `asap-telegraf`. The patched OTAP submodule
# depends on a sibling `asap-precompute-rs` checkout (path-dep at
# `../asap-precompute-rs/` from the staged registration crate); doing
# the full Cargo build inside Docker would require either mounting
# that sibling into the BuildKit context or vendoring it into the
# image, both of which complicate iteration. Like the `asap-otel`
# parallel, this Dockerfile is just a runtime stage that wraps the
# pre-built binary.
#
# ## Prereqs (run once on the build host)
#
# 1. Initialize the upstream submodule so the patches can be applied
#    on top:
#
#      git submodule update --init --recursive otel-arrow
#
# 2. Build the binary (sets the GOPRIVATE-equivalent Cargo env vars
#    inline — see build_asap_otap.sh's "Env vars" section):
#
#      bash build_asap_otap.sh
#
#    Binary lands at
#    `otel-arrow/rust/otap-dataflow/target/release/asap-otap`.
#    Verify the plugin registry:
#
#      ./otel-arrow/rust/otap-dataflow/target/release/asap-otap -h \
#        | grep asap_sketches
#    # Expects: ...urn:asap:processor:asap_sketches...
#
# 3. Build this image (the COPY below expects the binary to be
#    present in the build context):
#
#      docker build -f deploy/docker/Dockerfile.asap-otap \
#        -t asap/asap-otap:dev .
#
# ## Runtime config
#
# OTAP Dataflow consumes a YAML/JSON pipeline config; mount it at
# `/etc/otap/config.yaml` (the entrypoint default). The
# `asap_sketches` processor accepts the TOML/JSON shape documented
# in `otap-patch/plugins/asap_sketches/sample.toml` and the
# crate-level rustdoc in `otap-patch/all/mod.rs`.

FROM debian:bookworm-slim
RUN apt-get update && \
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends ca-certificates && \
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

COPY future-support/otap/otel-arrow/rust/otap-dataflow/target/release/asap-otap \
    /usr/local/bin/asap-otap

# The OTAP runtime exposes its admin/HTTP server on the
# `--http-admin-bind` address (no fixed default); receivers/exporters
# in the user config bring their own ports. Expose the canonical OTLP
# / OTAP gRPC + HTTP ports so a stock pipeline config "just works."
EXPOSE 4317 4318 8888

ENTRYPOINT ["/usr/local/bin/asap-otap"]
CMD ["--config=/etc/otap/config.yaml"]
